---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Add a repository, merge or package to pyproject.toml

Usage: odx add [OPTIONS] <SPEC>

Arguments:
  <SPEC>
          `owner/repo#PR`, `owner/repo@REF`, a pull request URL, or `URL#PR` / `URL@REF`

Options:
      --package <DIST>
          Add as package DIST instead of as a merge

      --subdirectory <DIR>
          Subdirectory of the addon in the repository (packages)

      --group <GROUP>
          Dependency group of the package

      --odoo-version <SERIES>
          Odoo series for a new [tool.odx] table

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve git repositories and forge and index data from the cache only; what is not cached fails. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Say when each repository's fetch and build starts, and what each fetched and merged

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on standard error: no progress lines, no warnings

Examples:
  odx add OCA/pos#123            merge a pull request (the repository is added if new)
  odx add OCA/pos@17.0-fix       merge a branch, or @<sha> a commit
  odx add OCA/pos#45 --package odoo-addon-pos_vouchers --subdirectory pos_vouchers
                                 one addon of a pull request as a package
